  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development would result in the loss of a family sized unit (4b 5p minimum), thereby failing to comply with policy H11.1 of Merton Local Plan 2024",
    "In the absence of an Air Quality Neutral Statement,\r\nthe applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development would be at\r\nminimum air quality neutral, not worsening local air quality thereby failing to\r\ncomply with policy SI1 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The development has failed to provide sufficient\r\nsecure, integrated, convenient and accessible cycle parking facilities,\r\ncontrary to policy T16.2 of&nbsp; Merton&#39;s\r\nLocal Plan 2024 and T5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The application has failed to demonstrate a net\r\ngain in biodiversity by incorporating ecologically friendly measures, as such\r\nis contrary to, in particular, Policy G6 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "In the absence of a Fire Safety Strategy\r\nincorporating but not limited to a plan detailing appropriate positioning of\r\nfire appliances and appropriate evacuation assembly points the scheme fails to\r\nprovide a safe form of development for future users contrary to, in particular,\r\nPolicy D12 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "In the absence\r\nof a completed S106 undertaking to ensure that scheme is prevented from being\r\nable to obtain residents and business parking permits for the Controlled\r\nParking Zone, the proposal would result in an increased demand for on street\r\nparking, resulting in a detrimental impact on highway and additional parking\r\npressure locally and be contrary to the Mayor and the Council&#39;s commitment to\r\nreducing car usage and promoting more sustainable forms of transport. The\r\nproposal would therefore be contrary to policy T6 of the London Plan 2021,\r\npolicy T16.1 and T16.2 of Merton’s Local Plan 2024."
  ],
